Original commit body from d8f936d:

Migrate GLSL, WGSL, COBOL, Fish, and GDScript analyzers to use the
shared NameResolver framework for cross-file call resolution:

- GLSL: Two-pass analysis with NameResolver for function calls
- WGSL: Two-pass analysis with NameResolver for function calls
- HLSL: Add pragma comments for defensive code paths
- COBOL: NameResolver for PERFORM/CALL resolution
- Fish: Two-pass analysis with cross-file function resolution
- GDScript: Two-pass analysis, fix bug where edge src was file ID

All analyzers now properly:
- Use caller function Symbol ID (not file ID) as edge source
- Use resolver.lookup() for callee resolution
- Assign confidence 0.85 * lookup_confidence for resolved calls
- Assign confidence 0.70 for external/unresolved calls

Also fixes generate-architecture to remove code fences from both
Structure and Configuration sections for better markdown rendering.

